From 1b22f812661fcea37bcacea5e7f139b3d9301112 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:17:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): validate launch classes against executing
 profile policy [daveey]

Preclaim used the actual worker profile registry but final tier application used the default-home registry. A disabled home registry cleared the chosen class and retained an old task selector at launch. Use the executing assignee registry at final class check. Ready legacy-row and sibling-progress controls now pass; retained independent-review control still has an obsolete exact-Opus expectation while the real resolver chooses independent Sol. Full focused assignment+declaration suite36pass1fail; group stopped at two iterations without weakening that remaining assertion. Capacity profile fixture5pass; full scripts/check21gates green. Not published or live proof.
